# Luau Style Guide

## Naming

Functions use PascalCase.

```lua
function Cannon:Fire()
end

function Cannon:GetState()
end
```

Variables use camelCase.

```lua
local currentYaw
local reloadState
local cannonState
```

Constants use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.

```lua
MAX_ROTATION
DEFAULT_FIRE_RATE
```

Module names use PascalCase.

```lua
CannonManager
CannonReload
FastCastProvider
```

Types use PascalCase.

```lua
type CannonState = {
    ...
}
```

---

## Formatting

Leave one blank line between functions.

Prefer early returns.

```lua
if not state then
    return
end
```

Never write

```lua
if state then
    ...
end
```

when an early return is possible.

---

Keep functions short.

Aim for under 40 lines.

Split large functions into helper methods.
